WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.259 --> 00:00:01.684
Since we are in New York,

2
00:00:01.684 --> 00:00:04.473
I thought I'd invite a very familiar voice.

3
00:00:04.473 --> 00:00:07.874
He's the voice of the New York Subway System.

4
00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:08.816
You hear him.

5
00:00:08.816 --> 00:00:11.111
(cheering)

6
00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:12.536
You hear him on all the trains

7
00:00:12.536 --> 00:00:14.253
and you hear him on the subway platforms

8
00:00:14.253 --> 00:00:16.015
and I wanted him to come out and just say hi.

9
00:00:16.015 --> 00:00:17.867
Please welcome Charlie Pellett!

10
00:00:17.867 --> 00:00:20.117
(cheering)

11
00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:24.059
Hey!

12
00:00:24.059 --> 00:00:24.982
Hiya, Charlie.

13
00:00:24.982 --> 00:00:25.817
Wow.

14
00:00:25.817 --> 00:00:26.769
(cheering)

15
00:00:26.769 --> 00:00:30.307
Charlie, you have an iconic voice.

16
00:00:30.307 --> 00:00:31.140
Lay it on us.

17
00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:32.719
You know what we want to hear, lay it on us.

18
00:00:32.719 --> 00:00:35.440
Stand clear of the closing doors, please.

19
00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:37.690
(cheering)

20
00:00:42.005 --> 00:00:43.236
That's fantastic,

21
00:00:43.236 --> 00:00:44.319
but, Charlie,

22
00:00:45.265 --> 00:00:47.327
Charlie, this is New York.

23
00:00:47.327 --> 00:00:48.427
That's way too polite.

24
00:00:48.427 --> 00:00:51.065
If you don't mind, say it like a real New Yorker, just once.

25
00:00:51.065 --> 00:00:51.898
You want to hear that?

26
00:00:51.898 --> 00:00:52.731
I say do it.

27
00:00:52.731 --> 00:00:56.125
Stand clear of the closing doors, please, or don't.

28
00:00:56.125 --> 00:00:57.177
Let's be honest,

29
00:00:57.177 --> 00:00:59.403
a guy with his head stuck in the subway doors

30
00:00:59.403 --> 00:01:01.319
would be pretty freakin' funny.

31
00:01:01.319 --> 00:01:02.152
All right.

32
00:01:02.152 --> 00:01:03.867
(applause)

33
00:01:03.867 --> 00:01:04.700
This is why we have you.

34
00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:05.955
Before you go,

35
00:01:05.955 --> 00:01:07.293
I thought of a couple of other phrases

36
00:01:07.293 --> 00:01:09.041
I've always wanted to hear in your voice.

37
00:01:09.041 --> 00:01:09.874
Do you mind?

38
00:01:09.874 --> 00:01:11.022
Can you do it right now?

39
00:01:11.022 --> 00:01:13.022
Next stop, funky town.

40
00:01:16.928 --> 00:01:18.761
Hey girl, you up?

41
00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:25.136
Just a reminder, we're all one day closer

42
00:01:25.136 --> 00:01:28.303
to those big closing doors in the sky.

43
00:01:31.455 --> 00:01:35.595
If you're taking this eastbound seven train to Citi Field,

44
00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:37.500
let me save you the trip.

45
00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.667
The Mets lose!

46
00:01:42.016 --> 00:01:43.326
Yeah, yeah.

47
00:01:43.326 --> 00:01:45.151
Stand clear of the closing doors

48
00:01:45.151 --> 00:01:49.536
and stand clear of your mind closing its doors,

49
00:01:49.536 --> 00:01:53.305
because life is a circle, time is infinite,

50
00:01:53.305 --> 00:01:56.285
and you have both never existed

51
00:01:56.285 --> 00:01:58.619
and always existed.

52
00:01:58.619 --> 00:02:01.250
(cheering)

53
00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:02.748
Charlie Pellett from Bloomberg Radio

54
00:02:02.748 --> 00:02:04.126
and New York Subway.

55
00:02:04.126 --> 00:02:05.376
Thank you, sir.

